<area shape="rect" id="node2" title="ddd.models.component.Declaration

One entry of the ``interface`` list of a component.
" alt="" coords="1057,1477,1583,1589"/>
<area shape="rect" id="node3" title="ddd.models.constants.ConstantDeclaration

One named integer constant, declared once and named wherever a shape needs it.
" alt="" coords="1235,2015,1405,2127"/>
<area shape="rect" id="node4" title="ddd.models.types.ExternalType

A name for a c type that DDD does not declare: a hand written header defines it.

DDD generates no typedef for it and knows neither its layout nor its meaning &#45; which is
the point: a driver&#39;s status word or an operating system&#39;s handle already has one
authoritative definition, and a copy of it in the description would drift. &#160;Only a
structure member may name one, as opaque storage that reaches the generated structure
verbatim; such a member states no unit, conversion or limits, because DDD does not check
meaning it cannot see.
" alt="" coords="1209,1826,1431,1966"/>
<area shape="rect" id="node5" title="ddd.models.types.ScalarType

A name for what a number means, so components agree by naming rather than by copying.

Three components consuming an engine speed each used to write out the datatype, the unit,
the scaling and the limits, leaving DDD to notice when one of them was wrong. &#160;If all three
say ``Speed_t`` instead, there is nothing left to disagree about &#45; which is checking turned
into construction.

It fixes exactly the four things that make two declarations interchangeable, and nothing
else. &#160;``kind``, ``dimensions``, ``init``, ``volatile`` and ``a2l`` stay on the variable:
they are properties of one object rather than of the type, and two measurements of the same
type may well differ in whether an interrupt writes one of them.
" alt="" coords="1765,5,2288,229"/>
<area shape="rect" id="node6" title="ddd.models.types.StructType

One structured datatype: a name and the members it lays out, in order.
" alt="" coords="1203,1638,1437,1778"/>
<area shape="rect" id="node8" title="ddd.models.objects.Axis

Shared axis points; several curves and maps may be interpolated over one axis.
" alt="" coords="1728,278,2325,754"/>
